Published here with permission.  They are provided by Pertti Eerikainen of
Finland.(eerikpe@sicom.fi)  A note from him on the Jenkka:
(me)> What's a jenkka?
(Pertti)> Difficult question...hmmm. It's quite similar with polka, tempo
is slower, beat is normally 2/4 or 4/4 can be also "alla breve" . Peoples dance it
with pairs first straigth and with twirl and then straigth etc...
somehow... I'm lousy dancer. It's very popular dance here in Finland.
(He is also not a native English speaker.)

