Bibliography
JGCW    John of the Greeny Cheshire Way. John Offord 1985
Friends of Folk Music, 55 Kingsway, London SW14
PDM     Complete Playford's Dancing Master. ed. Jeremy Barlow 1985
Faber Music 3 Queen's Square London WC1N 3AU
FofH    the Fiddler of Helperby. James Merryweather / Matt Seattle 1994
Dragonfly music, 10 Gibson St, Newbiggin-by-sea, Northumberland NE64 6PE
MR              1000 English Country Dance Tunes. Michael Raven 1984
26 Church Lane, Derrington, Stafford.
RHB(1)  Tune book of Mary Richards Darowen. Robin Huw Bowen 1991
Arfryn, Moreia, Capel Seion, Aberystwyth, Dyfed, SY23 4EA, Wales
RHB(2)  Tro Llaw (100 Welsh Hornpipes) Robin Huw Bowen 1987
National Library of Wales, ASBN 0-907158-25-0
CMTB    Charlton Memorial Tunebook. A. Hall \& WJ Stafford.
Northumbrian Pipers Society.
KV              Kiall Vannin (A source book of Manx tunes) Colin Jerry 1987
Slieu Shilley, 6 Glenfaba Rd, Peel, IOM
KM              the Kershaw Manuscript, Jamie Knowles, 1994
YDW     Bowen \& Shepherd - Tunes \&c from the 1798 mss of Joshua Jackson,
pub Yorkshire Dales Workshops, ISBN 1-897925-17-4
See also
Northern Lass (Mallinson Music).
Great Northern Tunebook (3 vols) (Dragonfly).
Northern Frisk (Dragonfly).
Northumbrian Pipers society tunebooks, etc etc
See also 'Westmorland.abc', which contains overlapping versions ...
I'll note these later when I get round to it.

